WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:14.276
Cheese Database turns scientific research papers into structured, reviewable research data. Each project keeps its papers, extracted evidence and scientific results together in one workspace.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:23.914
After uploading a research paper, the platform analyzes the document while keeping the original paper available for inspection.

00:00:25.309 --> 00:00:34.117
Tables, figures and relevant scientific evidence are captured directly from the paper, while preserving their connection to the original source.

00:00:35.478 --> 00:00:45.390
The extraction layer converts this evidence into structured scientific information, including experimental conditions, treatments and reported measurements.

00:00:46.782 --> 00:00:57.174
Researchers remain in control. Extracted observations can be inspected, edited, approved or rejected before they become trusted data.

00:00:58.566 --> 00:01:08.382
The platform also preserves the scientific structure behind the measurements, connecting each study to its experiments, treatment arms and observations.

00:01:09.571 --> 00:01:21.595
Approved observations flow into a searchable scientific database. Only fields that are relevant to the paper need to appear, avoiding unnecessarily sparse datasets.

00:01:22.781 --> 00:01:30.989
The resulting dataset can then be exported in common formats for further analysis, modelling or research workflows.

00:01:32.487 --> 00:01:49.047
From the original research paper to structured, traceable data, Cheese Database keeps the evidence, scientific context and researcher review connected throughout the workflow. Built for research that needs to remain inspectable, structured and reusable.
